  "title": "The Arrow That Was a Fish",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "perception and hidden objects",
  "premise": "A traveler follows a painted arrow through a gallery, but it repeatedly appears to point back toward the entrance. Walking around the freestanding sculpture reveals that the supposed arrow is a flat fish silhouette viewed end-on; a separate clearly labeled route sign finally leads to the exhibit.",
  "hook": "The directions have a tail.",
  "visible_action": "Camera orbits a narrow sculptural profile; arrowhead becomes a fish fin; body widens; traveler spots the real route marker.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Check whether an apparent instruction is actually a sign.",
  "gate": "Design and verify the exact camera-dependent silhouette; do not rely on changing the sculpture between shots.",
